    "turn_file": "/shared/3/projects/podcasts/transcriptionQueue/turns/pol_appearance_episodes_interviews/9/5/95626.jsonl",
    "turn_idx": 9,
    "turn_text": "Yeah, it's not so much that. So what you'll see if you go is you'll see in the exhibit hall pavilions from countries around the world and from states who are all basically saying, Come and build a biotechnology company where I live. It's about economic development. These are high paying jobs. It's a growing industry. We lead the world. So there's that. The other thing you'll see is a room with 500 or so numbered booths, little 10 by 10 rooms, and people who want to do business deals, they want to talk CEO to CEO or they want to talk investor to company Big company, the little company. They search the various participants. They invite them to a one-on-one and then with our proprietary system, we schedule it. We'll put on 50,000 one-on-one meetings in the course of a few days where people will create new collaborations, partnerships and deals and relationships.",
