    "turn_idx": 14,
    "turn_text": "Yeah, the science is really galloping right now. exciting is immunotherapy where our bodies evolved immune systems to fight bacterias and to fight viruses, but it's never really been able to fight cancer. Well, now we've got drugs that have basically enabled our immune system to attack cancer cells and cancer tumors and treat cancer that way. I remember Jimmy Carter had a cancer that had metastasized into his brain a couple of years ago where we thought he was going to die. When he received immunotherapy, he's treated, he's cured, and he just had a little tumble yesterday. Well, Turkey hunting, so I guess he seems to be doing fine. We have a company in Philadelphia called Spark Therapeutics that came to understand how it is that a disease that was making children go blind, that resulted from a genetic mutation, they were able to take the correct genetic sequence that the children were missing, inserted into viruses that can then deliver those genetic materials into the interior of the cells behind the eyes and render the children able to see again. And so, and that's called gene therapy. It's the first one ever approved by the FDA, and we expect to have another 40 or so in the pipeline, treating all kinds of diseases.",
