    "turn_idx": 18,
    "turn_text": "Yeah. Well, I think the bottom line is we're going to be able to use it against every form of cancer. Cancer cells change, and mutate, and it sounds as if they're intelligent, they're not. But by the random mutations, they're able to constantly fend off the immune system and prevent it from attacking their cells, the cancer cells. So what we've done, basically, is tricked. We've forwarded their protective system. and therefore we can enter their structure and defeat the cancer. So there's no limit to our ability to go after all kinds of cancer, because, of course, cancer isn't one thing. Cancer is dozens and dozens of diseases, and each one of them is somewhat unique. And so turning the individual's immune system against their individual kind of cancer is really quite remarkable.",
