  {
    "episode_id": 95626,
    "turn_file": "/shared/3/projects/podcasts/transcriptionQueue/turns/pol_appearance_episodes_interviews/9/5/95626.jsonl",
    "turn_idx": 23,
    "turn_text": "Right. And what I have suggested, looking at the Medicare program, and I was in Congress when we created the prescription drug benefit for Medicare, which hadn't existed prior to 2003, what I've suggested is that that we step up, I think the insurance company should step up, and we pay for it. Don't put it on the taxpayers. We can contribute to helping to close that gap so that people, the beneficiaries on Medicare, aren't at risk of not being able to get to medicine they need. So this is one where I think we ever step up to the plate, and I'm encouraging my companies and my association to do that.",
